Basic relationship:
f: A (Domain, definitionsmängd) -> B (Range, Värdemängd) is a rule that to every x in A yields one function value f(x) in B
Function graph/Funktionsgraf/Funktionskurva: {point(x, y): y=f(x)}
$math{Domain D_f (set, allowed x values) -> Range V_f (set, based on allowed domain values)}
Algebraic form of function: f(x) = <rule> <bound>, function contains expression and bound (as domain D_f), to every x in domain map to one y in range.
(<bound> can be omitted, and implicitly defined as the largest possible set of real numbers) e.g. f(x)=1/sqrt(x), <bound> infers to x>=0
Continous: The function is continuous for all x in the domain.

One to one mapping function, (x_1, x_2 in D_x)
f: A->B
$math{\\A x_1!=x_2 -> f(x_1) != f(x_2)} or $math{f(x_1)=f(x_2) -> x_1=x_2}

$math{root(x, n)} as inverse function to f(x)=x^n if odd, f(x)=(x^n:x>=0) if even, n in N, n>=0
$math{x^(1/n)=root(x, n)}
$math{x^(m/n)=(x^(1/n)^m \\A m}

Check f injective
$math{f(x)=y => x=g(y) => f^(-1)(x)=g(x)}
Verification: $math{f(f^(-1)(x))=x}

$math{f(x) = \\S{k=0, n, a_k*x^k}}
Degree: The highest exponent of a variable in a polynomial indicates the degree of the polynomial.
Standard form: $math{f(x) = \\S{k=0, n, a_k*x^k}}
Intercept form: $math{f(x) = a*\\P{k=0, n, x-r_k}}

Every polynomial eqn f(x) = 0 has n roots x_1, ..., x_n, if k equal roots are counted k times
Each difference (x - x_1) is a factor of f(x):
$math{f(x) = 0 = (x - x_1)(x - x_2)...(x - x_n)}

Presetted values:
$math{f(x) = x^3 + x^2 + 2*x + 2 = 0}
f(x) sign changes = 0
=> # of positive roots = 0

$math{f(-x) = -x^3 + x^2 - 2*x + 2 = 0}
f(-x) sign changes = 3
=> # of negative roots = 3 or 1

$math{f(x) = x^3 + x^2 + 2*x + 2 = 0}
has at least 1 negative root
=> by inspection x_1 = -1
therefore $math{f(x) = (x + 1)(x^2 + 2) = 0}
=> $math{x_2 = sqrt(2)*i, x_3 = -sqrt(2)*i}
